# The racer CSI driver registration.
#
# racer's CSI driver has no controller service and there is no
# external-provisioner sidecar anywhere in this deployment. Provisioning a
# racer volume means allocating extent ids and an LBA range out of a
# universe's global address space, which is cluster-scoped state that
# unbounded-operator already owns; handing that to a second leader-elected
# process would give the address space two writers. So the operator stamps
# the allocation onto the PersistentVolume as an annotation, and the node
# driver's job is only to turn an already-allocated volume into a block
# device on the node that needs it.
#
# That shape is what the CSIDriver object below declares:
#
#   attachRequired: false      There is no ControllerPublishVolume. A racer
#                              volume is not attached to a node; it is
#                              *composed* on a node, at NodeStageVolume, by
#                              adding a Device entry to that node's config.
#                              Leaving this true would make the kubelet wait
#                              forever for a VolumeAttachment nobody creates.
#
#   podInfoOnMount: false      The driver makes no decision that depends on
#                              which pod is mounting.
#
#   fsGroupPolicy: None        Block volumes have no filesystem to chown.
#
#   volumeLifecycleModes:      Persistent only. An ephemeral inline racer
#     [Persistent]             volume would need allocation at mount time,
#                              which is precisely the thing the operator owns.
#
# The default StorageClass is deliberately not here. A StorageClass whose
# provisioner is racer.unbounded-cloud.io *is* a racer universe, and the
# operator records the universe id, catalog size, epoch, LBA cursor and
# per-zone membership in annotations on that object. Server-side applying it
# from a manifest on every reconcile would strip the annotations the same
# field manager wrote by patch, so the operator creates the class once, in
# Go, and then leaves it alone. See ensureDefaultClass in
# internal/operator/components/racer/allocate.go.
---
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: CSIDriver
metadata:
  name: racer.unbounded-cloud.io
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: racer
spec:
  attachRequired: false
  podInfoOnMount: false
  fsGroupPolicy: None
  volumeLifecycleModes:
    - Persistent
